messages:
nina_sales: Marta on the Zenith POC reported flaky streaming in their embedded webview. They see parser exceptions and mid-stream disconnects during the transcript feed. Demo paused.
raj_se: Can you grab the browser network log and any client stack traces? Is this only in the embedded webview or also in desktop browsers?
marta_customer: Only in our android webview wrapper so far. Desktop Chrome looks fine. Posting clipped client log: "Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input at parseSse (sse.js:210)". Network shows SSE events arriving but some data lines are cut mid-object.
sam_oncall: Infra notes: I see a cluster of TCP resets from the load-balancer around the same period, plus a burst of 429 responses from our gateway for that API key. LB logs: "connection reset by peer while reading upstream". Also a few proxy buffer-full warnings.
raj_se: sounds like two contributing causes: (A) client assumes each SSE data: payload is a complete JSON message and calls JSON.parse immediately, (B) network/proxy resets or buffering cause data frames to be truncated. If the webview concatenates chunks differently from Chrome, that explains the platform variance.
marta_customer: Example stream snippet from devtools (copied):

event: message
data: {"seq":10,"text":"Part1 of a long

"}

event: message
data: {"seq":11,"text":"continued part that got trun

"}

client error occurs on second data payload. We tried enabling retries in the wrapper but it made things worse.
raj_se: Immediate workaround for you: modify the SSE handler to buffer consecutive data lines until a full JSON parse succeeds. Also set the wrapper's HTTP client to avoid aggressive connection drops: increase socket timeout and disable intermediate retries for streaming endpoints.
sam_oncall: On our side I'll temporarily lower retry concurrency for that org and disable automatic proxy buffering for streams to reduce mid-frame fragmentation. I'll also push a keepalive heartbeat (comment line ":
") every 12s from canary to keep connections active.
deploy-bot: canary release v2.15.0 deployed to eu-central-1 at 2104122200
nina_sales: Marta, do you want us to apply the infra tweak now and share a tiny patch you can drop into the wrapper?
marta_customer: Yes please. Patching the wrapper is slow, so a server-side quick fix would be ideal.
aj_se: I can post a tiny JS accumulator snippet you can paste into the wrapper's SSE callback; it doesn't need a full rebuild: 
```js
let acc = ''
function onDataLine(line) {
  acc += line;
  try {
    const obj = JSON.parse(acc);
    handle(obj);
    acc = '';
  } catch (err) {
    // incomplete, wait for more data
    if (acc.length > 64 * 1024) { acc = ''; console.warn('dropping oversized partial'); }
  }
}
```
Also recommend a short timeout to flush buffer if no progress after 5s.
sam_oncall: Action items: (1) infra: reduce retry concurrency for org zenith (done), disable proxy buffering for SSE endpoints (applied to canary), add heartbeat comments (in progress). (2) se: share accumulator snippet (done). (3) sales: coordinate with customer to drop snippet in wrapper and increase socket keepalive.
nina_sales: Thanks team. Marta will try the canary infra changes and the snippet and report back. Marking this POC as high-touch until the exec demo completes tomorrow.
marta_customer: Applying proxy change now, will test in ~20m and upload results here. Appreciate quick turnaround.
